  "notes": "The employees-by-country table in the Annual Report 2025 (Sustainability Report, 'Employees and non-employees') covers 73 countries and territories at Dec 31, 2025 and sums to its stated total of 602,659 (614,082 a year earlier). It excludes the Chinese joint ventures; including them, the Group had 662,942 employees. Côte d'Ivoire and Hong Kong appear as rows in the 2025 table; Belgium fell from 3,561 to 782. The Group management report also gives employees by market including the joint ventures, which is not recorded because it is on a different basis. The report says the production network encompassed over 111 production sites including the Chinese joint ventures, 67 of them vehicle production plants, but there is no machine-readable plant list, so plants are not counted by country. Sites are named in the report text; the Wolfsburg headquarters address (Berliner Ring 2) is quoted from the report's voting-rights notices. The report has no U.S. state breakdown, and no taxes-by-country table (only Group and divisional income taxes paid). A separate Volkswagen tax transparency report was not checked.",
